{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the angel of YHWH appeared to him.</b> In a prophetic vision. For truly, when angels manifest in the likeness of men outside of prophecy — as with Abraham, Lot, Balaam, and others — Scripture does not say of them וַיֵּרָא (\"appeared\"), but rather וַיַּרְא (\"he saw\"), as in: וַיַּרְא וְהִנֵּה שְׁלֹשָׁה אֲנָשִׁים (Genesis 18:2), וַיַּרְא לוֹט (Genesis 19:1), וַיַּרְא אֶת מַלְאַךְ ה' נִצָּב בַּדֶּרֶךְ (Numbers 22:31)." "<b>And he looked, and behold, the bush burned with fire.</b> Burning. This is the mode of prophetic riddle: the angel was within the bush, and the fire burned in the bush around the angel, to signify that while the righteous of Israel — who are the angels of YHWH — are within the bush of the Egyptian people, who were to them thorns and brambles, that bush would be consumed by fire through the affliction of the ten plagues, yet they would not be consumed by those afflictions, as He signified by saying \"and the bush was not consumed\" — it was indestructible in the blazing fire kindled within it. For the prophecy of Moses our master, peace be upon him, was not then as it would be afterward, as he testified by saying \"for he was afraid to look upon Elohim\" — the opposite of וּתְמוּנַת ה' יַבִּיט (Numbers 12:8). But from the day of the giving of the Torah onward, when He was revealed to all Israel face to face and they could not bear it, as they said: לֹא אֹסִף עוֹד לִשְׁמֹעַ אֶת קוֹל ה' וגו׳ (Deuteronomy 5:22), and he alone remained at that level, as it says: שׁוּבוּ לָכֶם וְאַתָּה פֹּה עֲמֹד עִמָּדִי (Deuteronomy 5:27–28), and as it says: וַיַּעֲמֹד הָעָם מֵרָחֹק וּמֹשֶׁה נִגַּשׁ (Exodus 20:18) — from then the prophecy of Moses our master was face to face, a vision and not in riddles."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:12.709725563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}